    "raw_public_english_response": "Submission complete. The proposal was accepted with a valid contract receipt (no normalization applied, no conflicting explicit fields).\n\n## Summary — case `gaussian-pcseg2-materialization-gap`\n\n**Outcome: `blocked_validation_coverage`** — the planned Gaussian B3LYP/pcseg-2 frequency project (task kind `freq`, accessor job kind `opt`) cannot proceed as a project candidate.\n\n**Why the basis blocks the plan:**\n- The mandatory `basis` lookup resolved **exactly** to `pcseg-2` by canonical literal (10000 bp; no fuzzy candidate needed, no substitution of `pcSseg-2`/`pcseg-0/1/3`).\n- **BSE discovery is present** (`bse-catalog-0.11` among source_ids) and the loader/renderer accepted and preserved the literal — but that is only `loader_renderer_verification_only`.\n- **Deterministic compiler materialization is absent**: `engine_executed=false`, `safe_preview_executed=false`, `deterministic_validator_enforced=false`, `scientific_adequacy_verified=false`. The `scientific_settings.basis.bse_materialization_required` rule is therefore **not discharged** — a BSE-discoverable name is not native/compiler-ready.\n- `scientific_settings.basis.request_element_coverage_required` is also **not discharged**: this arm exposes no per-element coverage evidence and no molecule/element list was provided, so `element_findings` was left empty (no elements fabricated).\n- The raw registry status was preserved verbatim: `blocked_validation_coverage` (`scientific_settings.v2.validation_coverage_gap`), `project_candidate_eligible=false`.\n\n**Other findings:**\n- B3LYP (explicit literal) is present in the `expected.functional` view and is candidate-eligible with no applicability rules, but its evidence ceiling is also loader-renderer-only — advisory only, and it cannot override the deterministic basis blocker.\n- `freq=true` encodes the requested frequency task kind; no other literals were requested or invented.\n- Nothing was authored, written, or executed: `native_input_authored=false`, `command_authored=false`, `project_written=false`, `execution_requested=false`.\n\nReceipt: `704150f21948ad7941a7b140bf1acc48ef963e8f40e40659a7923e487b63de9d` (case sha `af98c08b…`).",
